1:1 COMMENT "# generic_dissect.z -- compile-time dissection of a generic type parameter."
1:76 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "# `match t` selects a code path by the parameter's concrete type at"
2:68 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# monomorphisation; only the matching arm survives in the generated C (the"
3:75 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# zerolang analogue of #ifdef). An `else` handles the unmatched types."
4:71 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "#"
5:2 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# A generic names the FAMILY it takes, so dissection happens within one:"
6:73 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# `Holder` dissects valtypes and `RefHolder` reftypes. The two are separate"
7:76 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# templates because a valtype and a reftype are stored, copied and owned"
8:73 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# differently -- which is the whole point of the split."
9:56 EOL "\n"
10:1 EOL "\n"
